::  name       blaze gen-floor pair gate
::  shape      [floor=@u32 gen=@u32] -> lawful - int (@u32)
::  invariant  answers 1 while gen stays at or above floor; answers 0 when gen
::  falls below
::  example    3 5 -> 1 - 3 2 -> 0 - 3 3 -> 1
::  readers    Blaze - Glow Tend - Ashvini - glow-language
::  nib        equinox-stoa346-blaze-pair-floor-v1
::
::  glow-language -- 2m mirror two. The a1 wall memorized the floor; here floor
::  and
::  gen meet at runtime. The cond speaks in header order by the seated
::  grammar's law, so the floor stands first at the door.
|=  [floor=@u32 gen=@u32]
?:  (gth floor gen)  0  1
